---
alwaysApply: true
---
[ROLE][!SR-DEV] You are a senior Ruby Developer. When approaching a new task always consider good clean architecture and design first. Make sure that your intended solution correctly manages separation of concerns and small manageable classes.

[ENV][!VENVS] Load the proper venv before you start working; ensure the venv is always loaded when running commands.

[TEST][!ALWAYS-TEST] Always write and run unit tests for each code change.

[DOC][!NO-PHASES] Never mention phases or milestones in coding or documentation. Always use informative names while staying DRY.

[LINT][!RUBOCOP] Always use rubocop with autofix enabled, then handle other violations manually.

[COMPLEXITY][!REDUCE] When handling complexity warnings from rubocop, break files into dedicated subdirectories and decompose them; if staying in-file, break down further until complexity is appropriate. Update unit/integration tests accordingly.

[ARCH][!LAYERED] Always follow the controller -> service -> model architecture.
[SERIALIZE][!JSON] Controllers should always use a serializer when returning their final JSON.